# Package Policy

When installing packages:
- Use stable versions.
- Prefer latest stable version compatible with the current Node.js LTS.
- Avoid deprecated packages.
- Avoid packages with low maintenance or security risks.
- Prefer official or widely-used libraries.
- Check if the package is actually needed before installing.
- Do not add multiple libraries for the same purpose.
- Update package.json scripts when needed.
- After install, run lint, type-check, and build.

Preferred packages:

Backend:
- @nestjs/*
- prisma
- @prisma/client
- argon2 or bcrypt
- helmet
- class-validator
- class-transformer
- @nestjs/throttler
- pino or winston
- zod if needed

Frontend:
- next
- react
- tailwindcss
- shadcn/ui
- react-hook-form
- zod
- @tanstack/react-query
- zustand
- lucide-react
